{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305125,"nonce":"S0LRAm5C6ZV2JDqVmOgPPj1XoXw=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhexg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/8","origin":"github"},"title":"Infohash is recomputed by re-encoding the decoded dict instead of slicing the original bytes","message":"```python\nhash = hashlib.sha1(bencode.bencode(info)).hexdigest()\n```\n\nThis decodes the torrent and then re-encodes the `info` dictionary to hash it. That only yields the correct infohash if the round-trip is byte-exact. It is not guaranteed to be: any non-canonical ordering or padding in the original, or any lossy bytes-to-str conversion by the decoder, produces a different hash.\n\nThe infohash must be `sha1()` over the **raw bytes of the info value as they appear in the file**, which means the parser has to report that byte range.\n\nThe wrong hash is then used to look up the save path in the qBittorrent config, so it fails silently by finding nothing.","files":null}]}